; Sidecar B for usealias_scope.scaly (loaded via `module usealias_scope_b`).
; Has its OWN free `helper` (returns 2) and a bare call to it. Sibling module A
; imports `nsx.helper` (returns 99); before the ModuleStack scoping fix, A's
; alias "helper" -> "nsx" bled through the global use-alias list and mis-mangled
; B's bare `helper(5)` as `_ZN3nsx6helperEi`, so `b_uses()` returned 99 instead
; of 2. With per-module push/pop scoping, B sees no such alias -> free
; `_Z6helperi` -> 2. Run standalone it prints PASS.
; Expected: PASS

function helper(x: int) returns int
    2

function b_uses() returns int
    helper(5)

print("PASS")
